    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/1/51873.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 37,
    "turn_text": "I don't know. My daddy and I, my dad was pretty cool. He would, on Saturdays or Sundays, one or the other, he would take me hunting or fishing. And on the other day, he would work with my brother on his, on one of his car projects or motorcycles. And, you know, going dove hunting, but, you know, I can remember coming up here along these coves and along the lakes, they were fishing with a poppin' bug and catching blue gi on. Of course, we'd always put in a Choto Marina. Way down. I remember we'd leave the house on Sundays. We'd always say we're going to do it early. We'd always end up being four o'clock. And I have vivid memories of holding up stringers of bluegill. We'd get home and we'd clean 40 or 50 bluegill and occasionally get a catfish. Daddy would always fish for bass, you know, but most of the time he was just trying to make sure I got to get the hook out of my head or something. But I always remember the one time he My buddy Chris Haggerty and I were fishing with him, and we, and Daddy's prized fishing rod. It was a Mitchell Garcia, fell off into the water. And we got out and we swam for it and couldn't find it. And Daddy said, all right, I'm going to do one more time. And because it was getting dark this Sunday, we had to be in school Monday morning. And Daddy, and then he hung it right on the end of the tip and brought it in. And I still have that rod three over this day. And because I remember I said, Lord, He can just get this. I remember praying. And Dad said, you know, I prayed about it. I didn't want to bother God. It's just a fish and rod. But now I have that fish and rod and reel, and I'll give that to my daughter. And that's a pretty cool memory. Because it was just, you know, And I can tell you how many catfish pulling a fishing pole into the water and jumping in and my buddy Sonny Parton and I were fishing one time down with my dad and of course when dove season would open we would get with it. But anyway, I would remind people this weekend do not drink and drive especially on the water. You'll end up losing your life or causing somebody else to to perish or get hurt. Anyway, I want to thank you so much for being on another episode of Tennessee Talks, and let's keep our state beautiful, and you all do it, and you keep it fun, and it's really cool, and I appreciate you being with me, Jeffrey. Thank you. Thank you, guys. I appreciate you all sending me here.",
